<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This story is a little bit personal, and for that I apologize. It's based on some actual shit I've dealt with and seen (particularly the bits with the judge). I've never been admitted into a place like this, but I've been in Lindsey's position enough times in my life to get a vague notion of what's going on inside them.</p>
<p>I'm definitely not here to start up a conversation about psychiatry in America — and my heart goes out to anyone working in the field (it's certainly a thankless task, and I've meant enough wonderful psychiatrists to know they exist, they're saving lives, and they need as much support as we can bear to provide them with). But some of these places fucking terrify me. In part, I wrote this SCP to try and show you why.</p>
<p>There's no final twist, no skeleton in the closet, no 'they were ghosts all along!'. Cragstaff is just all the misery I've seen in these places poured into one horrible fucking hole. And that hole will never, ever let you leave.</p>
<p>I have no idea if the two of them made it out. I hope they did.</p>
