Regarding Julia's mental health records:
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Julia went in as a teenager. Speaking from real life experience: Tracking down mental health history records for someone back when they were a teenager can be <em>absurdly</em> hard, if not literally impossible. And that's when the person in question gives you permission! It gets even more ridiculous if the mental health institute has since closed. Harder still if you don't know what you're looking for. And on top of all that, states have different requirements for how long they're required to keep these documents &#8212; they may have already been destroyed!</p>
<p>I imagine that, yeah &#8212; the Foundation has the resources to even retrieve documents <em>which no longer physically exist</em> &#8212; but they're not going to pull those resources out to screen every researcher they hire. They'd probably just do your standard screening and call it a day.</p>
<p>Lindsey dug way deeper &#8212; largely because she had good reason to.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
And as for Browning's assessment:
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>He's not saying to discount her testimony, he's just being a jerk and pointing out that the logs speak for themselves. He doesn't want to update the article to include direct mention of 'alt-dimension' Cragstaff because Julia's depiction is anecdotal; he brings up the schizophrenia mostly just because he's a fucking asshole.</p>
<p>He's not doubting she was taken by SCP-3054; he's merely doubting that her description of alt-dimension Cragstaff was accurate. Maybe that wasn't clear from his email? I don't know.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

