<p>I'm settling on an upvote. The logs develop nicely and are immersive. However, it is also fairly predictable in terms of the way in which Owens progresses as a character, as well as the resolution. The notion of a place with a constantly shifting internal layout has been done before on the site, and this doesn't offer anything new in that regard. Nevertheless, it is a well-crafted yarn.</p>

